WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.400
Here's the script that I have prepared for this round.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.660
It is my second tragedy, Macbeth.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.660
Are you ready?

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.290
Now then...

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.420
Let's open the curtains.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.970
"All hail Macbeth,"

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.220
"that shalt be king here after."

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.230
"Yet so shalt thou become an usurper and king-slayer."

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.030
She's trying to draw me into the play and turn me into Macbeth's actor!

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.280
"The line gets whacked away, into the ground!"

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.120
"Macbeth shall never be vanquished."

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.950
"And thus he takes another blow!"

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:26.750
"All hail Macbeth, free from harm until
Great Birnam Wood shall come against him."

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.340
Damn it! There is no end to this.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.260
I am going to push the story along.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.640
"Burning with desire be the woman who enticed her husband,"

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.220
"O the foolish Lady Macbeth."

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.390
C-Cecil, do you see that?

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.930
Focus on sharing your weight on that mechanical shell.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.190
Tes!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.360
A-A direct hit?

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.040
I-I can't move!

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:12.840
Swords?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.930
Inferior Frontal Synapses, fire away!

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.600
Gush out, youth!

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.810
Now!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.020
Oh, yeah!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:40.070
The Great Birnam Wood is after you, Macbeth.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.830
I'm still not—

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.290
Doesn't someone have to fill in as understudy when an actor goes down?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.210
You discharged all of these lines...

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.290
How did you secure the energy to pull that off?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.670
Curious?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.680
That's—

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:01.470
Tes.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.100
This is England's Armament of Deadly Sins, Aspida Philargia.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:11.110
It takes any damage dealt to its master

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.570
and transforms it into ether.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.110
Indeed, I am always taking a large amount of damage.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.910
Even you have lashed out at me, haven't you?

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:21.910
Critiques.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:24.290
"The premise for the world in this story is weak."

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.750
"There are contradicting points."

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.250
"This story is flawed."

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:29.710
"This part wasn't done well."

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.290
You're free to have your own opinion about my books.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.760
In the end, critiques are nothing more than intellectual essays on one's impressions.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.930
But those critiques give me power.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.180
There is something I forgot to ask you.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:44.970
What is it?

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:50.940
Tres España used to possess a secret church-run facility
that raised children too young to enter elementary school.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.900
It was an elite training operation linked with Henares' talented and gifted program.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.910
Thirteen years ago, a group of the children rebelled and destroyed the facility.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.830
Do you remember the 13th Mutsugorei Academy?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.790
I have finally found you, No. 13.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.290
No, I should use the name given to you to indicate your alliance with Musashi,

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.550
Toussaint Neshinbara.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.850
You hurt me back then as well!

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.640
Shit! Let go!

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.980
At this rate, I'm going to completely merge with Macbeth!

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.020
Go!

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.400
It's now or never!

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.650
"He sent me flying!"

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.780
Shinagawa, do it now!

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:46.780
Judge.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:54.960
What's this!?

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.510
They're entering orbit?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.600
Tch, time's up!

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.140
Mates, retreat!

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.820
Scarred, let's get farther back.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.860
We could get hurt if something flew out at us.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.030
Milton, do you hear something?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.030
Something besides the sound issued by Musashi?

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.250
This sound...?

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:39.840
Low speed anti-warship rounds!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.970
There was an enemy warship in stealth mode!?

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.680
Enemy fire from an unidentified warship has been confirmed.

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.490
Ether feedback from England's second level confirmed.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:08.950
I have identified it as the sword spell for local defense, Excalibur Caliburn.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:09.950
Over.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.170
Everyone, brace yourselves. Over.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.850
I play tennis!

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.430
Where's Aoi?!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.690
At this rate, we're going to crash into Takao.

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:41.610
To think that I should be the first to detect him.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.490
Futayo, I'm asking this as the Vice-President.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.530
Please sever the transport cables!

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.030
I'll explain everything to that idiot later.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.530
Judge. Masazumi, I am your ally.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.620
I will offer you a favorable testimony at the magistrate's office.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.080
Whatever! Just hurry.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.290
Judge.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:07:59.500
Destroy the evidence!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.920
Bind, Slicing Dragonfly!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.350
M-Madam Musashi, who is the one responsible for this battle?!

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.140
Master Konishi...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:17.020
I must have a word with him
about the commerce for this—

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.480
M-Madam Musashi, a-a naked
man fell from the sky!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.440
Oh, Koni! What are you doing here?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.530
He would have the highest authority in the matter.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.950
Feel free to talk all you want. Over.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.750
Futayo!

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.800
I won't make it in time!

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.590
Then I'll just have to alter the ship's path!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:49.220
That's—

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.760
He intends to strike the ship and alter its path!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.370
Are you all right?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.010
A scar from a sword...

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.630
What have you done!?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.930
There were still—

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.470
Take a closer look.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:36.850
Everyone here is okay.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:38.560
As is this child.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.600
You saved them...?

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.310
Isn't that great?

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.020
Um...

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.780
Um, well...

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.160
Wait!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.410
That's...

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:21.850
That attack a moment ago...

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.860
Master Tori, we have not received permission from England to dock.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.150
As such, our ship shall remain on standby at our present location.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.780
Furthermore, England is blocking all communication with the cargo ship. Over.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:35.530
Really?

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.530
So, then!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.660
What'll it take to see Horizon?

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.580
I believe we must wait to hear from England. Over.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.500
Excuse me!?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:50.090
H-H-Horizon!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.600
I caught one!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.810
She's tough!

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.230
Good, good.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.780
Just how long must we stay here?

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:20.080
I hope Aoi is negotiating to let us disembark.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:48.150
N-Now then, we shall hereby commence the emergency meeting

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:51.570
of Oxford Academy's Student Council and Supreme Federation.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:56.900
First on the agenda is how to handle the Far Easterners illegally residing in England.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:02.160
Gentlemen, do you not think we should take advantage of the cards in our hands?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.910
Let us use them as our Joker for the coming Spanish Armada.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.880
Thanks, miss!

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.750
Wow, it looks yummy!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.550
There is no need to push.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.300
There is still plenty to go around.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.010
Lady Juana,

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:25.810
aren't you going to distribute these treats to the other children?

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.890
No. When I suggested doing this,

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.730
he agreed on the condition that the treats be delivered

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:36.690
equally to Elves, Half Elves and humans.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:38.320
Tes.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:44.740
Lady Juana, why do you trust the Chancellor?

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.960
Gin, why do you trust Tachibana Muneshige?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.130
That's because...

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.960
Because he gave me a reason to live.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:13:01.220
Then there is no need for you to hear my answer.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.510
Besides, right now he has merely...

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:11.650
...lost his reason to live.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.690
Ah, found her! Miss!

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:20.360
England has finally come to a decision regarding Musashi.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.620
The cargo ship that crash-landed in their 4th Level area

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.370
still hasn't been given permission to return to Musashi.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:31.000
But apparently they've been granted permission to send the cargo ship supplies and go ashore on Level 4.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:35.460
They also want to hold a commerce meeting, but isn't that...?

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.340
It goes to show how close the reenactment of the Spanish Armada is.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:44.350
We are currently building the Grande y Felicísima Armada.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:49.020
How will England and Musashi perceive San Martin?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.730
Mitotsudaira!

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:59.230
I'll swap out with you.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.610
Oh, Masazumi!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.150
Futayo isn't going to relieve me?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.160
Apparently Futayo is serving as Horizon's bodyguard.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.700
Judge.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.950
And where is Horizon?

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.410
I don't know why,

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:15.250
but she's been sleeping nearly 20 hours a day since she got hit by Akidía Katárripsi.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.880
Even Horizon can't seem to discern why.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:22.260
Automated Dolls have it rough in their own right, don't they?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.550
At any rate,

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.550
these past two weeks have been quite the adventure.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:28.810
With both food and clothing problems,

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.270
I was worried what would become of us.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.140
But that master of outdoor survival has been quite the live-saver.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.900
Hey, you two!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:37.440
Speak of the devil...

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.940
I'll take over from here.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.610
You two ladies should go get your rest in preparation for tomorrow.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.740
Thank you. I shall take you up on that.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:52.620
Still, I wish we could bathe in water that wasn't boiling hot before bed.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.620
Yeah, same here.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.670
That won't be a problem!

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.170
I asked Shirojiro to take care of that for you.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.470
He's such a considerate guy,

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:07.890
so why does his history of no girlfriends equal the length of his life?

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.890
You! Watch what you say!

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:14.180
Hey, Horizon! Can you hear me?

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:18.610
So, uh, tonight Musashi and England are going to...

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.440
to... have national intercourse.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.400
Most impressive, foolish Brother.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.110
But it's supposed to be "diplomatic meeting".

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:28.240
Oh, amazing! You're a genius, sis!

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.330
But I like "national intercourse" better because it sounds pervy!

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.750
The countries will make out! They'll make out?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:34.330
I wanna see that meeting!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.460
Shut up! Do you know what time it is?!

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:37.250
I wanna see that meeting!

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.290
I-I bring havoc!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.090
Why is everyone acting normal?

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.340
There's another thread?

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:49.720
Sheesh.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:52.260
I'll get the attention-hog treatment until this heals up.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.810
They're making crap up...

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:59.350
I was just thinking I hadn't seen you for a while.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.230
What are you doing out here?

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:02.770
Naruze?

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:06.240
Judge. At least you remember that much.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.070
Shall we beaten dogs whimper and whine to each other?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.240
Whine, huh?

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:15.250
Didn't you have Asama purify that spell?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:19.330
This curse won't disappear until the play is over.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.710
Macbeth is a usurper who kills the king.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:25.710
So in my case, it's not going to disappear until I kill Aoi.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.840
That's why I'm keeping my distance from Aoi.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.470
I'm nabbing that theme!

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.260
Was that all you came for?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.480
No, we haven't complained yet, have we?

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.440
You're getting bashed like mad on the net, you know?

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.820
You understand the reason why, don't you?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.110
I didn't win. Isn't that right?

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:53.370
No matter how badly injured you get, the loss is given meaning if you win.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.620
But it's all for naught if you lose.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.620
Then you'll just have to win next time...

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.000
Using your own spells.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.790
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:06.960
So, what did you want to whine about, Naruze?

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:21.400
I wanted to show Naito that I would be okay on my own,

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:22.940
even without Weisse Frauen, but...

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.440
I think you fought plenty hard.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:33.990
But I don't think I was able to sweep away all of Naito's worries.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:35.870
It's humiliating,

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:39.410
but it just goes to show that I'm a third-rate actor who must exit the stage.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.000
You're still up on the stage.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:47.460
You should mull over on how to deal with that Macbeth curse for a while.

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:55.010
Jeez, why did she come see me?

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:06.150
Chancellor.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:09.230
G-Gin? M-May I help you?

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:13.450
Lady Juana is waiting to hand over the letters that were addressed to you.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:17.450
Excuse me, but is the person who frequently writes to you actually your lover?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:22.540
N-No! Those letters are from an Elven orphan.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.040
An Elf?

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:30.130
My only military gain in the Battle of Lepanto was rescuing that child.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.690
She's asleep.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.280
And she's even using compressed sleep talismans.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:58.580
Now then...

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.870
Letters, letters...

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.790
Keep calm! Gently...!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:08.210
Now!

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:10.500
Excuse me, I forgot—

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:21.310
I never thought you the type to ask Lady Juana, one of the Eight Great Dragon Kings,

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.430
to pretend she's asleep while you bow your head down into her crotch.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.100
You are truly a good guy.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.310
I wish Master Muneshige had such moves in that department.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:29.610
Well then, take care.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.980
Don't go!

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.990
Phew, it fell down.

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.370
Huh? Where's the one from the child?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.500
Normally God only puts you through one trial...

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.090
Why!?

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.470
Chancellor, after brief speculation,

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:07.310
I have come to realize that an adult man like yourself and a serious teacher-type such as Lady Juana—

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.400
Tes!

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.400
Let's just leave it at that.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.240
Too fast! You're judging too fast!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:22.830
You are a doubly good man to have Lady Juana pretend she's asleep

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.700
while you hold a boob-fiddling cabaret this time.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.210
I truly wish that Master Muneshige were a man of such devices.

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.460
Well, take care.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.710
I said not to go!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.860
Sorry for everything.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.950
"Dear Mister,"

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.120
"Mister, are you well? I am fine."

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.660
"Lately there are clouds in the sky."

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.290
"Mister, have you heard?"

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:13.000
"There are bunches of ships inside of those clouds."

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.500
"Everyone at the academy says,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.300
'War! War is coming!'"

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:22.180
"Mister, are you going to war?"

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.810
"Mister, you saved my life."

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.520
"I do not like war."

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:33.690
"But you and the other men saved me."

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:40.070
"If there is another war, will you save me again?"

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:51.960
"I tell people who are afraid of the word 'war' all about you."

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.460
"I tell them, 'No matter what happens, it will turn out okay because we have you.'"

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.090
"If there is another war,

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:02.550
Mister, will you save me again?"

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:06.560
"I hope that what I told them does not turn into a lie."

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:07.850
"That is how I feel."

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:14.060
Of course I'd go save you. I swear it.

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:18.150
But I'm not sure if the current general would...

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:22.860
Will I be able to protect you along with the country,

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.620
the people and all those things that matter this time?

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:43.090
I'm on my way over,

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:46.340
Horizon!
